course: dictionary
lesson: 995
title: Boggy ground
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Boggy means wet, soft and muddy, like a bog. When you walk on boggy ground, your feet sink in, so you need wellies and must go carefully.
explain: Use the words around it to check. «Most plants live quietly on light, air, water and a little from the soil, but some grow in wet, boggy ground so poor...» The word wet is a clue. Ask: what word would fit here? Try "wet and muddy" in the sentence, and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Boggy is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like «boggy ground», «a boggy field» or «a boggy path». You can also compare: boggier means more boggy, and boggiest means the most boggy.
fact: Boggy means wet, soft and muddy, like a bog.
fact: «Boggy» ground is soft and wet, so your feet can sink into it.
fact: Boggy is an adjective: it describes a noun, as in «a boggy path».
fact: Boggy land is common on moors in Ireland, Scotland and northern England.
fact: In stories, boggy land slows travellers down.
exercise: «In summer the tundra is bright day and night, boggy and buzzing with mosquitoes.» What does boggy mean here? | Dry and sandy | *Wet, soft and muddy | Tall and green | Hard and frozen
exercise: «It begins at its source, often a spring or a boggy patch in the hills.» What is a boggy patch? | A place where a river meets the sea | A dry rock with no plants | A tall hill covered in trees | *A small area of wet, soft, muddy ground
exercise: «Reindeer hooves are soft in summer for boggy ground and hard in winter to cut into ice.» Which ground are the soft hooves for? | Sand | *Boggy ground | Rock | Ice
test: In «some grow in wet, boggy ground», what does the word wet tell you about boggy? | *Boggy ground is wet and soft | Boggy ground is hot and sunny | Boggy means the same as tall | Boggy ground is dry and hard
test: What is a good way to check that you have understood boggy? | Skip the word and never come back to it | Ignore the sentence and guess | Look only at the first letter | *Swap in wet and soft, then see if the sentence still makes sense
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to boggy? | *Marshy | Tall | Sunny | Icy
